<title>VENEZUELA: Mobil signs 1.6 bln deal with Pequiven.</title>
<headline>Mobil signs 1.6 bln deal with Pequiven.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mobil Chemical Co, a unit of Mobil Corp, signed a $1.6 billion joint venture deal Thursday with Pequiven, the petrochemical wing of state-run Petroleos de Venezuela (PDVSA), to develop an olefins complex.</p>
<p>A &quot;preliminary development agreement&quot; was signed by Mobil Corp Executive Vice President Eugene Renna and Pequiven President Arnold Volkenborn at a public ceremony.</p>
</text>
